  "summary_en": "Conceptual paper arguing that the ethics of robots used in environmental research, protection and remediation has been neglected. It proposes a taxonomy of environmental robots (robots-in-ecology, robots-for-ecology, ecobots) and flags unique ethical and practical issues for follow-up work.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Environmental robotics is largely absent from the roboethics literature.",
   "Proposes a taxonomy: robots-in-ecology, robots-for-ecology, and ecologically-functional robots (ecobots).",
   "Defines environmental robots as service robots (ISO 8373) serving environmental research, engineering, protection or remediation.",
   "Calls for a 'green robotics' ethics, including the environmental burden of robot materials and disposal.",
   "Identifies ethical issues as subjects for future work."
